## ⚠️ Limitations

- Products are predefined in the Java source code.
- Cart information is stored in memory.
- Data is not saved after the application closes.
- Checkout is simulated; no real payment is processed.

## 📝 Conclusion

The Java E-Commerce Application is a beginner-friendly project that demonstrates basic online shopping functionality using Java. It helps students understand Java Collections, OOP concepts, and menu-driven application development.

